==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|velt|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|feld|lang=goh}}, from {{proto|gem-pro|felþan|lang=de}}. Cognates include Dutch {{term|veld|lang=nl}} and English {{term|field|lang=en}}.<ref>{{R:EWddS|ed=22|hw=Feld}}</ref>. German {{term|Gefilde||fields|lang=de}} is a collective derivation of ''Feld''.<ref>{{R:EWddS|ed=22|hw=Gefilde}}</ref>

